B.aE4=new A.ht(B.bg7,"Gain is not power. Every antenna here radiates the same power; more gain only moves it. Raise the gain and the pattern grows in one direction and shrinks everywhere else, which is why a high-gain omni leaves a hole under itself.",null)
B.yq=new A.as(57730,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.aE_=new A.ht(B.yq,"Gain and beamwidth trade directly. A rule of thumb: gain is about 31,000 divided by the two beamwidths multiplied together, in degrees. 41,253 is the ideal (the square degrees in a sphere); real antennas fall short of it.",null)
