B.QP=new A.ht(B.ap,"Every subcarrier is off. Turn one on to see a symbol.",null)
B.aDS=new A.ht(B.ap,"Every subcarrier is off, so there is no signal. Turn one on beside the stage.",null)
B.aDU=new A.ht(B.ap,"Five sines is the most this tool sums. Remove one to add another.",null)
B.aDV=new A.ht(B.ap,"Every amplitude is zero, so there is nothing to show. Raise an amplitude.",null)
B.aDX=new A.ht(B.ap,"The peak is the gain the file states. The rebuilt shape integrates to its own directivity; a gap between the two is losses in the real antenna, or the estimate between the cuts.",null)
B.aDZ=new A.ht(B.ap,"Every amplitude is zero, so every bin sits on the floor.",null)
B.aE0=new A.ht(B.ap,"Every subcarrier is off, so there is no signal. Turn one on in Subcarriers below.",null)
B.aE1=new A.ht(B.ap,"HE puts the subcarriers 4 times closer together (78.125 kHz instead of 312.5 kHz), so each symbol lasts 4 times longer (12.8 \xb5s instead of 3.2 \xb5s). Nothing about the carrier frequency changes: the channel center stays where it is, and a 20 MHz channel is still 20 MHz wide.",null)
B.aE2=new A.ht(B.ap,"Every amplitude is zero, so there is nothing to show. Raise an amplitude slider.",null)
B.aE3=new A.ht(B.ap,"Every amplitude is zero, so every bin sits on the floor. Raise an amplitude in Waves or pick a lesson.",null)
B.bfR=new A.as(63668,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.aE7=new A.fC(B.bfR,"RFC 5169: an EAP-TLS run needs at least 3, typically 4 or more, round trips.",null)
B.aE8=new A.fC(B.ap,"The fading spread is an illustrative setting, not a measurement: each reading is the model level plus a random draw with that standard deviation.",null)
B.bg2=new A.as(983633,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.aEa=new A.fC(B.bg2,"Not counted: the scan for the next AP. In measured handoffs (802.11b, open authentication; Mishra, Shin and Arbaugh 2003) the scan was over 90% of the delay. 802.11k neighbor reports shorten the scan; PMK caching and FT shorten only what this ladder shows.",null)
B.aEc=new A.fC(B.ap,"Model values, not measurements: ITU-R P.2040 walls (one solid slab each), ITU-R P.526 knife-edge diffraction, and reflections up to two bounces. No floor, ceiling, furniture or people.",null)
B.aEd=new A.fC(B.ap,"Absorption is the decay along the path inside the wall. Reflection is what the faces send back, including the way their echoes add or cancel in a thin wall or across an air gap. The two add up to the total before rounding.",null)
B.aEe=new A.fC(B.GR,"A 2D plan of a 3D model: the signal spreads in three dimensions (1/r), but there is no floor or ceiling bounce.",null)
B.aEf=new A.oy(B.ap,"Under this rule the client is set to the most it may transmit. The rule is a ceiling: many clients transmit less, which widens the gap.",null)
B.aEg=new A.oy(B.ap,"These sensitivities are conformance floors, the least a radio must manage to pass. Real radios do several dB better, so real rings are larger.",null)
B.h9=new A.as(62624,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.aEh=new A.oy(B.h9,"No class is on. Turn one on to read its EIRP, noise floor and SNR.",null)
B.aEi=new A.oy(B.h9,"No class is on. Turn one on to read its EIRP and SNR.",null)
B.aEj=new A.oy(B.ap,"Both ends use the same receiver floors (the conformance minimums for each MCS). Real radios do better than the floors, and many APs gain more on receive from extra antennas and receive chains, which this model leaves out.",null)
B.aEk=new A.oy(B.ap,"Every body loss here is an illustrative setting, not a measurement. No measured body-loss figure stands behind these defaults: set them to match what you measure.",null)
B.bfx=new A.as(62537,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.aEl=new A.oy(B.bfx,"No time to crack is shown: it depends entirely on the attacker's hardware.",null)
B.aEm=new A.oy(B.ap,u.eF,null)
B.aEn=new A.oy(B.ap,"The EU has no client offset: an LPI client may use the same 23 dBm as the AP, so there is no AP power to set.",null)
B.aEo=new A.oy(B.ap,"A 2x2 client uses at most two streams, so one phone alone may notice little. The AP loses the streams it could share among many clients at once and, with a radio off, a whole band.",null)
B.aEp=new A.oy(B.ap,"The count assumes the password was picked at random from these characters. A word, a name or a pattern is on every guess list and falls long before the count runs out.",null)
B.aEq=new A.oy(B.ap,u.c4,null)
B.QQ=new A.oy(B.ap,"Illustrative values: every device offset, grip and body loss, the AP power (14 dBm) and the path loss exponent (3) are examples for teaching, not measurements of any real device.",null)
