B.bXp=s(["Keith Parsons \xb7 CWNE #3","Written for US homes \xb7 September 2026"],t.s)
B.bsy=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/home-internet/cover.svg",700,250,null,null)
B.byh=new A.b3("Internet reaches your house in one of six ways. Five end at a box from your provider. A phone hotspot is its own box. Your Wi-Fi starts at the router, right after that box.")
B.bJq=new A.aS("This guide answers three questions. What are your choices? Why does it matter which one you pick? And what should you check before you sign up?",!1)
B.bqT=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/home-internet/fig-01.svg",644,184,"**Figure 1. Three things you're buying.** Speed, lag and a data limit are three different things.",null)
B.ak=new A.a4L(0,"note")
B.bor=new A.bC(B.ak,"A word on the words","Your **provider** is the company you pay. Their **box** is where their line ends in your house. The **router** plugs into that box and makes your Wi-Fi. Often one box does both jobs.",null,null,B.r)
B.bos=new A.bC(B.ak,"The one idea to remember","The service you pay for stops at the router. The Wi-Fi inside your house is a separate thing. A faster plan won't fix a slow back bedroom.",null,null,B.r)
B.c26=s([B.byh,B.bJq,B.bqT,B.bor,B.bos],t.X)
B.bDt=new A.aE("1","The short answer",B.c26,null)
B.bxK=new A.b3("A strand of glass, a cable TV line, an old phone line, a radio tower, a satellite dish, or your phone. Most end at the same place: a box in your house.")
B.buF=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/home-internet/fig-02.svg",700,330,"**Figure 2. Six ways in.** Five end at your provider's box; a phone hotspot is its own box. Everything right of the dashed line is yours, starting with the router.",null)
B.bIk=new A.aS("That handoff point matters. When something is slow, the first question is which side of the line the problem is on.",!1)
B.cfX=s([B.bxK,B.buF,B.bIk],t.X)
B.bEV=new A.aE("2","Six ways in",B.cfX,null)
B.bz8=new A.b3("No home gets a private pipe. Every kind of service shares something with the neighbors.")
B.bqJ=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/home-internet/fig-03.svg",700,250,"**Figure 3. What each option shares.** Fiber splits one strand among a group of homes. Cable shares one line along the street. A cell tower and a satellite beam each serve many homes at once.",null)
B.bI4=new A.aS("That's why the same plan can feel fast at noon and slow at eight at night. More neighbors are online.",!1)
B.btb=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/home-internet/fig-04.svg",644,226,"**Figure 4. Same plan, busier road.** In the evening more neighbors share the same road, so each home's share gets smaller. The lime part is yours.",null)
B.ch5=s([B.bz8,B.bqJ,B.bI4,B.btb],t.X)
B.bGa=new A.aE("3","Every road is shared",B.ch5,null)
B.byx=new A.b3("A wire into your house is usually the steadiest choice. Rain and snow don't slow it down.")
B.bsW=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/home-internet/fig-05.svg",644,292,"**Figure 5. Three kinds of wire.** Fiber carries light through glass, cable uses the TV line, and DSL uses the old phone line. Each one ends at a box inside your wall.",null)
B.bq0=new A.fo("Fiber","Light through a glass strand. The fastest, the quickest to answer, and it often sends as fast as it receives.")
B.bq5=new A.fo("Cable","The same line as cable TV. Fast downloads. Sending is much slower.")
B.bpZ=new A.fo("DSL","The old phone line. The slowest wired choice, and it gets slower the farther you live from the phone company.")
B.ck2=s([B.bq0,B.bq5,B.bpZ],t.UA)
B.bqF=new A.m7(B.ck2)
B.bvD=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/home-internet/fig-06.svg",700,220,"**Figure 6. Sending matters too.** Video calls, photo backups and cameras send data up. Fiber often sends as fast as it receives. Cable and 5G home internet send much less.",null)
B.bsw=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/home-internet/fig-07.svg",644,248,"**Figure 7. DSL slows with distance.** The same phone line gives slower service to homes farther from the phone company. Not to scale.",null)
B.hf=new A.a4L(1,"caution")
B.boM=new A.bC(B.hf,"DSL is going away","Phone companies are shutting down their old copper lines. If DSL is all you have, look now for other choices at your address.",null,null,B.r)
B.chH=s([B.byx,B.bsW,B.bqF,B.bvD,B.bsw,B.boM],t.X)
B.bF5=new A.aE("4","Wires to your house",B.chH,null)
B.bzf=new A.b3("No wire? A radio link can reach almost anywhere. It's more at the mercy of weather, trees and busy times.")
B.bri=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/home-internet/fig-08.svg",644,366,"**Figure 8. Four ways radio reaches a house.** Towers need a clear path, satellites need open sky, and the far satellite answers slowly. Not to scale.",null)
B.bq4=new A.fo("5G home internet","A box in your window talks to the same towers your phone uses. It slows down when the tower is busy.")
B.bpU=new A.fo("Local wireless","A small local company aims an antenna on your roof at its tower. It needs a clear view.")
B.bpO=new A.fo("Low-orbit satellite","A dish talks to satellites flying fairly low, like Starlink. Quick to answer, and it works almost anywhere with open sky.")
B.bpT=new A.fo("High-orbit satellite","A dish aims at one satellite far out in space. It works, but every answer takes a long trip.")
B.bYQ=s([B.bq4,B.bpU,B.bpO,B.bpT],t.UA)
B.bqH=new A.m7(B.bYQ)
B.brl=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/home-internet/fig-09.svg",700,170,"**Figure 9. Low orbit and high orbit.** Low-orbit satellites fly just above the Earth. A high-orbit satellite sits far out in space, so every answer takes much longer to come back.",null)
B.bHQ=new A.aS("A **phone hotspot** uses your phone's data plan. It's fine for a trip, or as a backup. It's a poor fit for a whole family.",!1)
B.bt0=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/home-internet/fig-10.svg",644,210,"**Figure 10. A hotspot is for one or two devices.** Your phone can share its data with a laptop on a trip. Sharing it with a whole house of screens is a poor fit.",null)
B.cjT=s([B.bzf,B.bri,B.bqH,B.brl,B.bHQ,B.bt0],t.X)
B.bGj=new A.aE("5","Radio to your house",B.cjT,null)
B.bxc=new A.b3("Speed is how much arrives. Lag is how long each answer takes to come back. They're two different things.")
B.bJO=new A.aS("Lag decides whether a video call feels natural or a game feels smooth. A faster plan barely changes it.",!1)
B.bs0=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/home-internet/fig-11.svg",700,250,"**Figure 11. How long an answer takes.** Wired service and low-orbit satellites answer quickly. A satellite far above the equator adds about half a second, which you notice on every call.",null)
B.bJl=new A.aS("Lag also rises when someone else in the house is streaming or uploading. That's normal. It rises most on DSL.",!1)
B.btA=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/home-internet/fig-12.svg",644,260,"**Figure 12. A busy line means a longer wait.** When someone uploads, your video call waits in line behind it. That wait is lag.",null)
B.bOG=s([B.bxc,B.bJO,B.bs0,B.bJl,B.btA],t.X)
B.bGx=new A.aE("6","Why lag is its own number",B.bOG,null)
B.byk=new A.b3("A speed test on your phone measures two things at once: your service and your Wi-Fi.")
B.bvb=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/home-internet/fig-13.svg",700,240,"**Figure 13. Two different measurements.** The provider's promise ends at the router. Your phone in the back bedroom adds the Wi-Fi on top. When the two tests disagree, the difference is your Wi-Fi.",null)
B.bwr=new A.ew("Test both ways")
B.c0r=s(["Plug a laptop into the router with a network cable. Run a speed test. That's the service you pay for.","Take the laptop or your phone to the room that feels slow. Run the test again over Wi-Fi.","Compare. If only the Wi-Fi test is slow, the fix is in your house, not a bigger plan."],t.s)
B.bGI=new A.hZ(B.c0r)
B.bry=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/home-internet/fig-14.svg",644,204,"**Figure 14. What the two tests tell you.** If only the Wi-Fi test is slow, fix the Wi-Fi. If the wired test is slow too, the service itself is slow.",null)
B.bXT=s([B.byk,B.bvb,B.bwr,B.bGI,B.bry],t.X)
B.bDk=new A.aE("7","The service, or the Wi-Fi?",B.bXT,null)
B.bwF=new A.b3("Start at the top, and stop at the first one you can get.")
B.buM=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/home-internet/fig-15.svg",700,250,"**Figure 15. Pick in this order.** Fiber first, then cable. Without a wire, try 5G home internet or a low-orbit satellite before the last choices.",null)
B.boi=new A.bC(B.ak,"Look up your address","The FCC's national broadband map shows which providers say they serve your home. If a listing is wrong, you can challenge it.",null,null,B.r)
B.bus=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/home-internet/fig-16.svg",644,204,"**Figure 16. See who serves your address.** Type your address on the FCC's national broadband map, then read the list. Names here are examples.",null)
B.bpw=new A.bC(B.ak,"Before you sign up","Every provider has to show a **Broadband Facts** label on its sign-up page. It's like a food label. Read it for the upload speed, any monthly data limit, and the real price after any promotion.",null,null,B.r)
B.brG=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/home-internet/fig-17.svg",644,396,"**Figure 17. Read three lines on the label.** The real price after any deal, the upload speed, and any monthly data limit. Simplified: a real label has more lines.",null)
