B.bEF=new A.aE("8","Which one should I pick?",B.bR2,null)
B.jD=new A.aS("Each myth is followed by what's true.",!1)
B.bAM=new A.ce("Slow in the bedroom means a slow internet plan.","Often it's the Wi-Fi. Test at the router first.")
B.bAR=new A.ce("A faster plan fixes lag.","Lag and speed are different things. More speed doesn't lower lag.")
B.bB0=new A.ce("Upload doesn't matter.","Video calls, backups and cameras all send data up. Cable and 5G send much less than they receive.")
B.bA3=new A.ce("Unlimited means unlimited.","Many plans slow you down after a monthly amount. The Broadband Facts label tells you where.")
B.brO=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/home-internet/fig-18.svg",644,290,"**Figure 18. The four myths in pictures.** Each picture matches a myth above, in the same order.",null)
B.ckf=s([B.jD,B.bAM,B.bAR,B.bB0,B.bA3,B.brO],t.X)
B.bCA=new A.aE("9","Four things people get wrong",B.ckf,null)
B.bIp=new A.aS("Checked on 27 September 2026. Provider plans change often. The Broadband Facts label is always the current word for your address. Prices are deliberately left out.",!0)
B.cc4=s(["FCC, Thirteenth Measuring Broadband America Fixed Broadband Report, FCC 24-136, Appendix C (2024; test period 2022): idle latency by technology, latency under load, DSL delivery of advertised speed, test boxes at the router","FCC Broadband Data Collection and National Broadband Map help pages: what the map shows, the December 2025 data, availability and location challenges","FCC Broadband Consumer Labels (fcc.gov/broadbandlabels) and FCC 22-7","Broadband Breakfast, 2026-01-13: AT&T approval to discontinue copper service","T-Mobile Home Internet FAQ and plans pages: typical speeds and data prioritization","Starlink Specifications (latency 25 to 60 ms on land; upload typically 10 to 30 Mbps)","ESA, Types of orbits (35,786 km, 22,236 miles); GPS.gov, Space Segment (20,200 km, 12,550 miles)","Speed-of-light arithmetic: 4 \xd7 35,786 km \xf7 299,792 km/s \u2248 0.48 s"],t.s)
