B.Y2=new A.b3("Each myth is followed by what's true.")
B.bAO=new A.ce("A nanosecond is too short to matter.","Light only goes about a foot in one. Wi-Fi times its turns in millionths of a second, so nanoseconds add up fast.")
B.bAP=new A.ce("Adding 3 dB doubles the power exactly.","It's close to double. That's close enough for any Wi-Fi math you'll ever do.")
B.bAx=new A.ce("A 100 Mbps plan downloads 100 megabytes a second.","Mbps means megabits. Divide by 8. At best, that's about 12 megabytes a second.")
B.bAK=new A.ce("A weak signal means something is broken.","A signal can arrive a billion times weaker than it left and still work. Wi-Fi is built for that.")
B.bvZ=new A.ew("Pictures to keep")
B.buD=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/scales-and-ratios/fig-11.svg",784,298,"**Figure 11. Four pictures to keep.** The four ideas from this guide worth remembering.",null)
