B.bui=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/wifi-on-planes/cover.svg",760,322,null,null)
B.bz2=new A.b3("Airplane mode turns off your phone's radios. Cellular is the one that matters in the air, so keep it off. If the airline allows it, you can turn Wi-Fi and Bluetooth back on.")
B.bJT=new A.aS("The plane's Wi-Fi works, but it feels slow. Everyone on board shares one link to the ground. Often that link goes through a satellite far out in space.",!1)
B.bHF=new A.aS("This guide answers three questions. What does airplane mode turn off? Why is plane Wi-Fi slow? And how do you get online in your seat?",!1)
B.boF=new A.bC(B.ak,"A word on the words","**Cellular** is your phone's link to your carrier's towers, for calls, texts and mobile data. **Airplane mode** is the switch that turns your radios off. Some phones call it **Flight mode**.",null,null,B.r)
B.c3T=s([B.bz2,B.bJT,B.bHF,B.boF],t.X)
B.bCT=new A.aE("1","The short answer",B.c3T,null)
B.byR=new A.b3("One switch turns off cellular, and usually Wi-Fi and Bluetooth too.")
B.bv3=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/wifi-on-planes/fig-01.svg",760,500,"**Figure 1. One switch, three radios.** Keep cellular off in the air. Turn Wi-Fi and Bluetooth back on only if the airline allows it.",null)
B.bvQ=new A.ew("Check the top of your screen")
B.bIF=new A.aS("Here's the surprise. Your phone remembers what you did last time. If you turned Wi-Fi on during your last flight, it may stay on next time.",!1)
B.bvm=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/wifi-on-planes/fig-02.svg",760,216,"**Figure 2. Your phone remembers your last flight.** Left, last time: you turned Wi-Fi back on. Right, this time: airplane mode leaves it on.",null)
B.bK0=new A.aS("So take a quick look at the top of your screen. The Wi-Fi or Bluetooth symbol means that radio is on. You should see no signal bars and no carrier name.",!1)
B.br0=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/wifi-on-planes/fig-03.svg",760,232,"**Figure 3. What to look for.** Signal bars, or 5G or LTE next to the carrier name, mean cellular is still on.",null)
B.ca0=s([B.byR,B.bv3,B.bvQ,B.bIF,B.bvm,B.bK0,B.br0],t.X)
B.bCB=new A.aE("2","What airplane mode turns off",B.ca0,null)
B.bwE=new A.b3("Most people think phones upset the plane's instruments. In the US, the main rule is about the cell towers on the ground.")
B.buS=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/wifi-on-planes/fig-04.svg",760,470,"**Figure 4. A phone in the air sees too many towers.** On the ground, hills and buildings limit how many towers your phone reaches. Up high, nothing is in the way. Not to scale.",null)
B.bL6=new A.aS("A phone up high can reach many cell towers at once. That would jam up the network for people on the ground. So US rules ban using cellular in the air.",!1)
B.bHJ=new A.aS("Wi-Fi and Bluetooth are a different story. Each airline decides which gadgets are fine to use. That's why the rules can change from one airline to the next.",!1)
B.bJK=new A.aS("When the crew gives an instruction, follow it.",!1)
B.c35=s([B.bwE,B.buS,B.bL6,B.bHJ,B.bJK],t.X)
B.bDw=new A.aE("3","Why the rule exists",B.c35,null)
B.bzb=new A.b3("Inside the cabin, the Wi-Fi is ordinary Wi-Fi. The hard part is the next step, from the plane down to the ground.")
B.brc=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/wifi-on-planes/fig-05.svg",760,530,"**Figure 5. Three ways down to the ground.** Towers work over land. Satellites also work over oceans. The far-away satellite adds the most delay. Not to scale.",null)
B.bJN=new A.aS("Over land, some planes talk to special towers that point up at the sky.",!1)
B.bJg=new A.aS("Over oceans, planes use satellites. Some satellites fly low and close. Others sit very far away, about 36,000 km (22,000 miles) up.",!1)
B.bwX=new A.b3("The far ones are the slow ones. Your message has to travel all the way up and back down, and so does the reply.")
B.br1=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/wifi-on-planes/fig-06.svg",760,640,"**Figure 6. The long way round.** Your message and its reply each go up to the satellite and back down. Follow the numbers 1 to 4. Not to scale.",null)
B.bJ6=new A.aS("A far-away satellite adds a delay you can't fix from your seat. On one of Keith's flights across the Atlantic, every test message took more than half a second to come back.",!1)
B.bRc=s([B.bzb,B.brc,B.bJN,B.bJg,B.bwX,B.br1,B.bJ6],t.X)
B.bEU=new A.aE("4","How the internet reaches a plane",B.bRc,null)
B.bxf=new A.b3("Every phone, laptop and tablet on board shares one link to the ground. At home a few people share your internet. On a plane, it's everyone.")
B.bsx=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/wifi-on-planes/fig-07.svg",760,540,"**Figure 7. Everyone on board shares the link.** The same link, cut into a few wide lanes at home and many thin slices on a plane. Not to scale.",null)
B.bvW=new A.ew("What works, and what doesn't")
B.bsg=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/wifi-on-planes/fig-08.svg",760,598,"**Figure 8. Small jobs fit in your slice. Big ones don't.** Each bar is how much of the link a job needs; the dashed line is your share. Not to scale.",null)
B.bWY=s([B.bxf,B.bsx,B.bvW,B.bsg],t.X)
B.bE1=new A.aE("5","Why it feels slow",B.bWY,null)
B.byo=new A.b3("Plane Wi-Fi usually has no password. You join it, and a sign-in page pops up. It asks you to pay, log in or accept the terms.")
B.bsf=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/wifi-on-planes/fig-09.svg",760,416,"**Figure 9. How the sign-in page appears.** Your phone checks whether it's online. The plane's network answers with its sign-in page instead.",null)
B.bHY=new A.aS("Some airlines give free Wi-Fi to members of their frequent-flyer club. Free still means signing in, so wait for the page and log in.",!1)
B.bvR=new A.ew("When the sign-in page won't appear")
B.bKW=new A.aS("Open your web browser and go to any web page. The sign-in page usually shows up. If the airline gives a web address, type that instead.",!1)
B.bso=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/wifi-on-planes/fig-10.svg",760,440,"**Figure 10. Open a browser; don't tap Cancel.** Left: going to any web page brings up the sign-in page. Right: on an iPhone, Cancel disconnects you.",null)
B.bIK=new A.aS("On an iPhone, don't tap Cancel on the sign-in screen. That disconnects you, and you have to join again.",!1)
B.cao=s([B.byo,B.bsf,B.bHY,B.bvR,B.bKW,B.bso,B.bIK],t.X)
B.bF_=new A.aE("6","Getting online in your seat",B.cao,null)
B.bzZ=new A.ce("Airplane mode always turns off Wi-Fi and Bluetooth.","It always turns off cellular. If you turned Wi-Fi or Bluetooth on last time, your phone may leave them on.")
B.bBo=new A.ce("Airplane mode is only about the plane's instruments.","In the US, the main rule protects cell towers on the ground. Each airline decides about gadgets.")
B.bBn=new A.ce("Plane Wi-Fi comes from towers on the ground.","Some does, over land. Over oceans it comes from a satellite.")
B.bBc=new A.ce("Free Wi-Fi means no sign-in.","Free usually means a free membership and a login. If the page doesn't pop up, open your browser.")
