B.btn=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/captive-portals/cover.svg",616,360,null,null)
B.bwD=new A.b3("That Wi-Fi sign-in page has a name: a captive portal. It sits between the Wi-Fi and the internet. Until you finish it, almost nothing else loads.")
B.bKT=new A.aS("This guide answers three questions. What is that page? Why does it matter to you? And what do you do when it won't show up?",!1)
B.bpc=new A.bC(B.ak,"A word on the words","People call it a sign-in page, a login page, a splash page or a captive portal. They all mean the same page. This guide calls it the **sign-in page**.",null,null,B.r)
B.bpE=new A.bC(B.ak,"Other guides in this series","Plane Wi-Fi has its own guide: __Wi-Fi on Planes, Explained__. For a TV stick or game console on the road, see __Travel Routers, Explained__.",null,null,B.r)
B.bLe=new A.kB("wifi-on-planes-explained",null,null)
B.zk=new A.kB("travel-routers-explained",null,null)
B.c6y=s([B.bwD,B.bKT,B.bpc,B.bpE,B.bLe,B.zk],t.X)
B.bGw=new A.aE("1","The short answer",B.c6y,null)
B.bxz=new A.b3("Joining the Wi-Fi and reaching the internet are two separate steps. A sign-in page stops you between them.")
B.btx=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/captive-portals/fig-01.svg",616,360,"**Figure 1. Full bars is only step one.** Your phone joins the Wi-Fi first. The road to the internet stays closed until you finish the page.",null)
B.bJU=new A.aS("That's why your phone can show full bars and still load nothing. The bars only tell you the Wi-Fi part worked.",!1)
B.bpi=new A.bC(B.d2,null,"\u201cIf a network ever asked you to sign in on a web page, your Wi-Fi already worked.\u201d","Keith's note",u.oI,B.r)
B.bvX=new A.ew("What the page asks for")
B.btz=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/captive-portals/fig-02.svg",616,250,"**Figure 2. Four common asks.** Most pages want one of these. Some only want you to tap Accept.",null)
B.bwl=new A.ew("Why places use one")
B.bIr=new A.aS("A place with free or paid Wi-Fi wants a say before you go online. It may check that you're a guest, show its rules, or charge for time.",!1)
B.bsM=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/captive-portals/fig-03.svg",616,270,"**Figure 3. Why places use one.** Hotels, airports, cafes and planes each have a reason. The page always comes first.",null)
B.c58=s([B.bxz,B.btx,B.bJU,B.bpi,B.bvX,B.btz,B.bwl,B.bIr,B.bsM],t.X)
B.bFA=new A.aE("2","A gate in front of the internet",B.c58,null)
B.byv=new A.b3("Your phone checks every new Wi-Fi network. It asks for a small test page it already knows by heart.")
B.buP=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/captive-portals/fig-04.svg",616,420,"**Figure 4. A test with a known answer.** A normal network sends the test page back. A sign-in network answers differently, usually by sending you to its own page. Your phone sees the wrong answer and pops the page up for you.",null)
B.bKe=new A.aS("You don't have to do anything for this check. It happens by itself, in a moment.",!1)
B.bw6=new A.ew("What you'll see")
B.bvE=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/captive-portals/fig-05.svg",616,380,"**Figure 5. Three ways the page shows up.** Each kind of device brings the page to you a little differently. Either way, finish the page.",null)
B.bIl=new A.aS("On an iPhone, tapping Cancel on the sign-in window takes you off the network. Finish the page first. If you cancel by mistake, just join again.",!1)
B.bIx=new A.aS("Email, messages and Wi-Fi Calling over that Wi-Fi wait for the page too. Regular calls over the cell network may still work.",!1)
B.bZA=s([B.byv,B.buP,B.bKe,B.bw6,B.bvE,B.bIl,B.bIx],t.X)
B.bED=new A.aE("3","How your phone notices",B.bZA,null)
B.byG=new A.b3("Sometimes the page never pops up. You're on the Wi-Fi, but nothing loads. Try these, in order.")
B.bQU=s(["**Give it a moment.** The page can take a few seconds to appear.","**Open your web browser and type an address that starts with http://,** such as http://example.com. The network can then show you its page.","**Forget the network, then join it again.** Your phone checks again from the start.","**Turn off your own VPN for a moment.** Turn it back on once you're signed in. For a work or school VPN, ask your IT team.","**Still stuck? Ask the front desk or the staff.**","**Need the internet right now?** Turn Wi-Fi off and use cell data, if your plan allows it."],t.s)
B.bGW=new A.hZ(B.bQU)
B.bqV=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/captive-portals/fig-06.svg",616,360,"**Figure 6. Start with http://.** A plain http:// address lets the network show its page. A secure https:// site can't be swapped, so your browser warns you instead.",null)
B.bqW=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/captive-portals/fig-07.svg",616,284,"**Figure 7. Forget, then join again.** This makes your phone check the network from the start.",null)
B.bws=new A.ew("If you use a VPN or private DNS")
B.bJX=new A.aS("A VPN (virtual private network) is an app that wraps up everything your phone sends. That can keep the sign-in page from reaching you. On Android, if Private DNS is set to a provider hostname, switch it to Automatic while you sign in. On an iPhone, a Private Relay message means you can turn it off for that one network.",!1)
B.btR=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/captive-portals/fig-08.svg",616,266,"**Figure 8. Off for a moment, then back on.** Switch the VPN off only long enough to finish the page, then turn it back on.",null)
B.bZX=s([B.byG,B.bGW,B.bqV,B.bqW,B.bws,B.bJX,B.btR],t.X)
B.bE7=new A.aE("4","When the page doesn't show up",B.bZX,null)
B.bzd=new A.b3("You signed in yesterday, and today the page is back. That's normal.")
B.bto=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/captive-portals/fig-09.svg",616,380,"**Figure 9. Two reasons the page returns.** Your time or pass ran out. Or your phone now shows the network a new Wi-Fi address, so it looks like a new guest.",null)
B.bJ_=new A.aS("Some phones change their Wi-Fi address from time to time. It makes you harder to follow from place to place. When the address changes, the network may not know you, so you sign in again.",!1)
B.bSz=s([B.bzd,B.bto,B.bJ_],t.X)
B.bEQ=new A.aE("5","Why the page comes back",B.bSz,null)
B.bza=new A.b3("Any Wi-Fi network can see some of what you do on it. A network with a sign-in page is no different.")
B.buj=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/captive-portals/fig-10.svg",616,360,"**Figure 10. Outside and inside.** Most sites now use secure pages, marked with a padlock. The network usually sees which site you visit, unless a VPN or a privacy setting hides it. It doesn't see what's on the page.",null)
B.bIe=new A.aS("A real sign-in page is a gate, not a window into your secure pages. Still, type only what the place needs.",!1)
B.clL=s([B.bza,B.buj,B.bIe],t.X)
B.bDz=new A.aE("6","What the network can see",B.clL,null)
B.bqK=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/captive-portals/fig-11.svg",616,280,"**Figure 11. A real page, and a trap.** A real page asks for a room number, a code, a login the place gave you, or a pass. A trap asks for the password to your email.",null)
B.bob=new A.bC(B.fi,"Never type your email password into a sign-in page.","A hotel or cafe doesn't need it. Fake networks use fake sign-in pages to catch passwords.",null,null,B.r)
B.btO=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/captive-portals/fig-12.svg",616,246,"**Figure 12. Check the network name.** A look-alike name can be a trap. Join the one the staff or the sign names.",null)
B.cg0=s([B.bqK,B.bob,B.btO],t.X)
B.bGg=new A.aE("7","Stay safe on the sign-in page",B.cg0,null)
B.bxZ=new A.b3("A TV stick, a game console or a smart speaker can join Wi-Fi. But many can't show you a sign-in page.")
B.bvd=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/captive-portals/fig-13.svg",616,360,"**Figure 13. No screen, no sign-in.** Ask whether the front desk can add your device. Or bring a travel router: it signs in once, and your devices join it.",null)
B.bJw=new A.aS("Some TV sticks let you finish the page on your phone instead. Check the device's help pages before you travel.",!1)
B.bHH=new A.aS("Travel routers have their own guide: __Travel Routers, Explained__.",!1)
B.bNG=s([B.bxZ,B.bvd,B.bJw,B.bHH,B.zk],t.X)
B.bDm=new A.aE("8","Devices with no screen",B.bNG,null)
B.bzT=new A.ce("Full bars means I'm online.","The bars only show the Wi-Fi part. A sign-in page can still be holding back the internet.")
B.bAy=new A.ce("The page broke, so the Wi-Fi is broken.","The page reached you over the Wi-Fi, so the Wi-Fi works. Open a browser to bring the page back.")
B.bAz=new A.ce("The sign-in page can read everything I do.","On secure pages, the network sees the site's name, not what you read or type.")
B.bzQ=new A.ce("Once I sign in, I'm set for the whole trip.","Time limits and a new Wi-Fi address can bring the page back. Just sign in again.")
B.bzN=new A.ce("A network with a sign-in page is a safe network.","The page is about who gets in, not about keeping you safe. Check the network name. A padlock means the link is private, not that the site is honest.")
B.btT=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/captive-portals/fig-14.svg",616,190,"**Figure 14. What the bars measure.** Full bars say you hear the Wi-Fi well. They say nothing about the internet.",null)
B.bYG=s([B.bzT,B.bAy,B.bAz,B.bzQ,B.bzN,B.btT],t.X)
B.bD7=new A.aE("9","Five things people get wrong",B.bYG,null)
B.bra=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/captive-portals/fig-15.svg",616,250,"**Figure 15. Arriving and leaving.** Finish the page before you count on your apps. Forget the network when you go.",null)
B.cmC=s(["**Get the network name from the staff or a sign.** Don't guess from the list.","**Join, and give the page a moment.** It usually pops up by itself.","**Finish the page before you count on email, messages or calls.**","**No page? Open a browser and type an http:// address.**","**Never give your email password to a sign-in page.**","**When you leave, forget the network.**"],t.s)
B.bGQ=new A.hZ(B.cmC)
B.c9T=s([B.bra,B.bGQ],t.X)
B.bDN=new A.aE("10","Tips for your next trip",B.c9T,null)
