B.bFZ=new A.aE("4","Every radio wave is analog",B.cfj,null)
B.bwN=new A.b3("Move away from the source, and every signal gets weaker. What you notice depends on the kind of signal.")
B.bsn=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/analog-vs-digital/fig-10.svg",784,400,"**Figure 10. A slope, a cliff and a staircase.** Wi-Fi sits in between: it slows down in steps to stay connected. A sketch, not a measurement.",null)
B.bHO=new A.aS("**Analog fades on a slope.** Old TV got snowy. FM radio gets more hiss the farther you drive.",!1)
B.bI5=new A.aS("**Digital TV drops off a cliff.** The picture looks perfect, right up until it freezes or disappears.",!1)
B.bI0=new A.aS("**Wi-Fi steps down a staircase.** As the signal weakens, Wi-Fi switches to a simpler, slower way of sending. It only drops you when even the simplest way fails.",!1)
B.boO=new A.bC(B.d2,null,"\u201cGet closer to the box. Walls, floors, furniture, and distance all chew up the radio signal between you and the box on the wall, and the further away you sit, the more gets chewed up.\u201d","Keith's note",u.h,B.r)
B.c37=s([B.bwN,B.bsn,B.bHO,B.bI5,B.bI0,B.boO],t.X)
B.bFB=new A.aE("5","Three ways a signal fades",B.c37,null)
B.bzL=new A.ce("Digital always sounds better.","Digital is better at copying and at ignoring noise. How good it sounds depends on how much of the sound it keeps.")
B.bB6=new A.ce("Wi-Fi sends ones and zeros through the air.","What travels is a smooth wave. The ones and zeros are in the small changes to that wave.")
B.bAB=new A.ce("Digital sound comes out of the speaker in steps.","Your phone smooths the numbers back into a wave before the speaker plays it.")
B.bAY=new A.ce("A weak digital signal just looks a little worse.","Digital TV usually looks fine until it stops. Wi-Fi slows down in steps instead.")
B.bv_=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/analog-vs-digital/fig-11.svg",784,180,"**Figure 11. The four facts, in pictures.** One picture for each fact above, in the same order.",null)
