B.byX=new A.b3("Some people use gadgets that drown out GPS. That's called jamming, and it's illegal in the US. Your dot freezes or disappears.")
B.bKu=new A.aS("A rarer trick sends fake satellite signals. That's called spoofing. It can move your dot to a place you've never been.",!1)
B.btL=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/how-gps-works/fig-12.svg",616,420,"**Figure 12. Two ways to fool GPS.** Jamming drowns out the real signal. Spoofing fakes it.",null)
B.bJz=new A.aS("You can't stop either one. If your dot looks wrong, trust your eyes and the road signs. Your phone falls back on Wi-Fi and cell towers where it can.",!1)
