B.bzR=new A.ce("GPS needs cell data.","Your position comes from the satellites alone. Data only helps it start faster and loads the map.")
B.bAl=new A.ce("GPS works indoors.","Mostly not. A roof blocks the signal. Indoors, your phone uses Wi-Fi and cell towers instead.")
B.bAU=new A.ce("My phone knows exactly where I am.","Outdoors, it's usually within about 5 m (16 feet). Near tall buildings or under trees, it can be off by much more.")
B.brn=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/how-gps-works/fig-13.svg",616,210,"**Figure 13. The circle around the dot.** A small circle means a close fix. Tall buildings make it bigger. Not to scale.",null)
