B.bvh=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/phone-data-abroad/cover.svg",700,250,null,null)
B.bxr=new A.b3("Your phone needs a plan that works where you're going. There are three ways to get one. And your phone number doesn't have to ride on the same plan as your data.")
B.bqO=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/phone-data-abroad/fig-01.svg",760,328,"**Figure 1. Three ways to get data abroad.** They differ in how you pay (the green row), whether you get a number, and what your phone needs.",null)
B.boj=new A.bC(B.ak,"The one idea that explains this guide","Most phones can hold two plans at once. Keep your home plan on for calls and texts. Let the second plan carry your data.",null,null,B.r)
B.bMe=s([B.bxr,B.bqO,B.boj],t.X)
B.bDB=new A.aE("1","The short answer",B.bMe,null)
B.bzg=new A.b3("A SIM holds a key. The phone network checks that key to know who you are and who pays the bill.")
B.bKd=new A.aS("A SIM card is the key on a small chip you slide in. An eSIM is the same key, downloaded into a chip already inside your phone. Many new phones only take eSIMs.",!1)
B.bvI=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/phone-data-abroad/fig-02.svg",760,262,"**Figure 2. Two ways to carry the same key.** A card and an eSIM reach the same towers. Neither one is a different network.",null)
B.bpI=new A.bC(B.ak,"A word on the words","**Carrier** means your phone company. **Roaming** means using a network your carrier doesn't own, usually abroad. **Unlocked** means your phone will take a plan from any carrier.",null,null,B.r)
B.bZI=s([B.bzg,B.bKd,B.bvI,B.bpI],t.X)
B.bFI=new A.aE("2","What a SIM does",B.bZI,null)
B.bz6=new A.b3("A phone bought from a carrier may be locked to it. Ask your carrier to get it unlocked well before you leave.")
B.bvG=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/phone-data-abroad/fig-03.svg",760,332,"**Figure 3. A locked phone won't take a travel eSIM or a local SIM.** On an iPhone, the Carrier Lock line tells you. \u201cNo SIM restrictions\u201d means it's unlocked.",null)
B.bsD=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/phone-data-abroad/fig-04.svg",760,218,"**Figure 4. No SIM tray means eSIM only.** Many new phones have no slot. A SIM card from an airport kiosk won't fit, so buy an eSIM instead.",null)
B.bS9=s([B.bz6,B.bvG,B.bsD],t.X)
B.bCS=new A.aE("3","Is your phone unlocked?",B.bS9,null)
B.byS=new A.b3("All three put your phone on a local cell network. What changes is who you pay, when you pay, and whether you get a phone number.")
B.buK=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/phone-data-abroad/fig-05.svg",760,300,"**Figure 5. Three roads to the same towers.** Each one bills you differently.",null)
B.bIt=new A.aS("Your carrier's plan is the easiest. A travel eSIM is usually the cheapest for data. A local SIM makes sense for a long stay, or when you need a local number.",!1)
B.cjo=s([B.byS,B.buK,B.bIt],t.X)
B.bGE=new A.aE("4","Three ways to get data",B.cjo,null)
B.byA=new A.b3("The simplest choice. Your phone joins a partner network when you land. Your carrier charges you by the day, or out of your plan.")
B.bKX=new A.aS("A daily fee sounds small. But it adds up on a long trip.",!1)
B.btc=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/phone-data-abroad/fig-06.svg",760,250,"**Figure 6. A daily fee adds up.** On a trip of over a week, a monthly travel plan usually costs less than paying by the day.",null)
B.bo_=new A.bC(B.hf,"What starts a day","Any call, text or bit of data on your home line can start that day's fee. That includes apps updating in the background.",null,null,B.r)
B.bHW=new A.aS("Check your carrier's travel page before you go. Plans and prices change often.",!1)
B.bXC=s([B.byA,B.bKX,B.btc,B.bo_,B.bHW],t.X)
B.bDZ=new A.aE("5","Roaming with your own carrier",B.bXC,null)
B.bzy=new A.b3("Both need an unlocked phone. Both are paid up front, so there's no surprise bill.")
B.bwj=new A.ew("A travel eSIM")
B.bIv=new A.aS("You pick a country, an amount of data and a number of days. It usually comes with data only, so that plan won't take normal calls.",!1)
B.br8=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/phone-data-abroad/fig-07.svg",760,130,"**Figure 7. A travel eSIM in three steps.** Set it up at home, switch it on when you land, and switch it off when you're back.",null)
B.bo1=new A.bC(B.hf,"Install it before you need it","Setting up an eSIM needs Wi-Fi or a hotspot. Do it at home, then leave it switched off until you land.",null,null,B.r)
B.bvU=new A.ew("A local SIM or eSIM")
B.bKo=new A.aS("Buy it online before you go, or at the airport when you land. It's good for a long stay or when you need a local number. You may need your passport.",!1)
B.ceX=s([B.bzy,B.bwj,B.bIv,B.br8,B.bo1,B.bvU,B.bKo],t.X)
B.bEM=new A.aE("6","Travel eSIMs and local SIMs",B.ceX,null)
B.byq=new A.b3("Your bank, your airline and your doctor all text your home number. So keep that line on.")
B.bvr=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/phone-data-abroad/fig-08.svg",760,270,"**Figure 8. One phone, two plans, two jobs.** Your home plan takes calls and texts. The travel plan carries the data.",null)
B.bw_=new A.ew("Where surprise charges hide")
B.bsq=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/phone-data-abroad/fig-09.svg",760,250,"**Figure 9. Your home line still rings abroad.** Data Roaming off doesn't stop any of these.",null)
B.bnZ=new A.bC(B.ak,"Calls home over hotel Wi-Fi","Wi-Fi Calling can carry your home number over Wi-Fi, often for free. Set it up before you leave. Our guide __Wi-Fi Calling, Explained__ covers it.",null,null,B.r)
B.c3e=s([B.byq,B.bvr,B.bw_,B.bsq,B.bnZ,B.zi],t.X)
B.bFq=new A.aE("7","Keep your own number",B.c3e,null)
B.bzC=new A.b3("Four switches decide what your phone does abroad. Each one stops something different.")
B.bv8=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/phone-data-abroad/fig-10.svg",760,306,"**Figure 10. Which switch stops what.** Data Roaming off stops data, but calls and texts still get through, and can still cost you. With Wi-Fi Calling on, calls and texts still work over Wi-Fi, even in airplane mode.",null)
B.bw5=new A.ew("The one to remember")
B.bKk=new A.aS("Turn **Data Roaming** off on your home line. On an iPhone it's in Settings \u203a Cellular. On Android, look in Settings \u203a Network. If your travel eSIM says to, turn it on for the travel line only.",!1)
B.boh=new A.bC(B.fi,"Know the emergency number","Learn the local emergency number before you land. It isn't 911 everywhere.",null,null,B.r)
B.c92=s([B.bzC,B.bv8,B.bw5,B.bKk,B.boh],t.X)
B.bFu=new A.aE("8","The switches that matter",B.c92,null)
B.bwH=new A.b3("Wi-Fi is often the cheapest data on a trip. It's also the least predictable.")
B.bon=new A.bC(B.d2,null,'"If a network ever asked you to sign in on a web page, your Wi-Fi already worked."',"In Keith's words","Keith Parsons, __Fix Your Own Wi-Fi__, chapter 6",B.r)
B.buL=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/phone-data-abroad/fig-11.svg",760,316,"**Figure 11. The sign-in page stands between the Wi-Fi and the internet.** Full Wi-Fi bars only mean step 1 worked. Nothing else loads until you sign in.",null)
B.bpN=new A.fo("Hotels","One internet line shared by every guest. Strong Wi-Fi bars can still mean a slow connection.")
B.bqi=new A.fo("Airports","A sign-in page and a crowd. Fine for messages. Don't wait until the gate to set up your eSIM.")
B.bpX=new A.fo("Cruise ships","At sea, your phone uses the ship's own service, and it costs extra. Keep Data Roaming off on board.")
