B.bvF=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/find-my/cover.svg",700,250,null,null)
B.bx9=new A.b3("Find My is one app that finds three kinds of things. It works on your iPhone, iPad, Mac and Apple Watch.")
B.bqb=new A.fo("People","Friends and family who choose to share where they are. Nobody is shared without saying yes.")
B.bqm=new A.fo("Devices","Your Apple gear. It can be found even with no signal, and even when it's switched off for a while.")
B.bpR=new A.fo("Items","AirTags and similar tags. They have no GPS. Other people's iPhones find them for you.")
B.c7a=s([B.bqb,B.bqm,B.bpR],t.UA)
B.bqu=new A.m7(B.c7a)
B.bof=new A.bC(B.ak,"The one idea behind all of it","An AirTag can't tell anyone where it is. It only whispers \"I'm here\" by Bluetooth. Any iPhone that walks past hears it and reports its __own__ location. That report is locked so only you can read it.",null,null,B.r)
B.bSI=s([B.bx9,B.bqu,B.bof],t.X)
B.bFz=new A.aE("1","The short answer",B.bSI,null)
B.bxj=new A.b3("Your suitcase is on a baggage cart. An AirTag is inside. Nobody has to do anything for what happens next.")
B.brC=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/find-my/fig-01.svg",760,300,"**Figure 1. The Find My network.** The tag whispers. A passing iPhone hears it and sends its own location, sealed. Only your devices can open it.",null)
B.bJy=new A.aS("A traveler walks by with an iPhone in a pocket. The phone hears your tag. It sends Apple its own spot, inside a sealed envelope. Your phone opens the envelope and shows a dot on the map.",!1)
B.bHZ=new A.aS("The traveler never knows. Apple can't read the envelope. Only you can.",!1)
B.cce=s([B.bxj,B.brC,B.bJy,B.bHZ],t.X)
B.bCF=new A.aE("2","How a stranger's phone finds your bag",B.cce,null)
B.bsa=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/find-my/fig-02.svg",330,150,"**Figure 2. The tag keeps changing its name.** Its radio ID changes every few minutes, so nobody can follow it by listening.",420)
B.bP1=s(["**The key stays with you.** Only your own devices can open the reports.","**The finder stays anonymous.** Apple doesn't know who found the tag, or whose it is.","**The tag keeps no history.** It doesn't store where it has been."],t.s)
B.bGT=new A.hZ(B.bP1)
B.c_Z=s([B.bsa,B.bGT],t.X)
B.bFS=new A.aE("3","Why it stays private",B.c_Z,null)
B.brI=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/find-my/fig-03.svg",760,290,"**Figure 3. Your dot is the finder's location.** The tag has no GPS and no Wi-Fi. The phone that heard it knows where it is, and that becomes your dot.",null)
B.bHP=new A.aS("So the dot moves only when someone walks by. In a busy airport, it moves all the time. In an empty field, it may not move for hours.",!1)
B.c2q=s([B.brI,B.bHP],t.X)
B.bEn=new A.aE("4","Where the dot comes from",B.c2q,null)
B.bxx=new A.b3("Far away, you see a dot on a map. In the same room, you play a sound. Up close, some iPhones show an arrow.")
B.bum=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/find-my/fig-04.svg",760,286,"**Figure 4. Three radios, three jobs.** The farther away the tag is, the rougher the answer. Not to scale.",null)
B.bIR=new A.aS("The arrow is called Precision Finding. It needs a special radio called Ultra Wideband in both the phone and the tag. Some budget iPhones leave it out. They can still see the map and play a sound.",!1)
B.boT=new A.bC(B.ak,"A word on the words","**Bluetooth** is the short-range radio your earbuds use. **Ultra Wideband** is a newer short-range radio that can tell distance and direction. It powers the arrow.",null,null,B.r)
B.bKy=new A.aS("A few countries switch the arrow off. There, you still get the map and the sound.",!1)
B.cc6=s([B.bxx,B.bum,B.bIR,B.boT,B.bKy],t.X)
B.bGh=new A.aE("5","Three radios, three jobs",B.cc6,null)
B.bqX=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/find-my/fig-05.svg",760,330,"**Figure 5. The four parts of the app:** People, Devices, Items and Me. A simple drawing, not a screenshot.",null)
B.bIo=new A.aS("Sharing your location is always your choice. You pick who sees it and for how long. You can stop any time.",!1)
B.buz=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/find-my/fig-06.svg",760,250,"**Figure 6. Three ways to stay in charge of sharing.** Pause hides you from one person, Check In tells a friend only if you're late, and one tag can be shared with the family.",null)
B.c3a=s([B.bqX,B.bIo,B.buz],t.X)
B.bDC=new A.aE("6","The app, and sharing with people",B.c3a,null)
B.byI=new A.b3("A phone with a flat battery can still be found for a while. So can one that's switched off.")
B.buk=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/find-my/fig-07.svg",760,170,"**Figure 7. Still findable.** With a signal, your phone reports itself. With a flat battery or switched off, it can still be found for a while through the Find My network.",null)
B.bII=new A.aS("Turn on {{Send Last Location}}. When the battery is almost gone, your phone sends its spot to Apple first. Step 1 at the back shows where.",!1)
B.boY=new A.bC(B.fi,"If a device is lost or stolen","Mark it as lost in Find My, from another device or at icloud.com/find. That locks it. Erasing it is the last step. **Apple will never contact you to say your device was found.** Never share your passcode or any code with someone who says they have it.",null,null,B.r)
B.bVg=s([B.byI,B.buk,B.bII,B.boY],t.X)
B.bFe=new A.aE("7","Your phone, even when it dies",B.bVg,null)
B.bzc=new A.b3("You can send an airline a live link to your bag's location. Many airlines accept it.")
B.bsQ=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/find-my/fig-08.svg",760,300,"**Figure 8. If your bag doesn't arrive.** Check the map, file the airline's report, then share the link. Showing your contact info is a separate switch.",null)
B.bw9=new A.ew("Before you fly")
B.buo=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/find-my/fig-09.svg",760,278,"**Figure 9. Before you fly.** Hide the tag inside the bag, and turn off its left-behind alert (Notify When Left Behind). Left: do this. Right: not this.",null)
B.c2d=s(["**Check the battery** in Find My. It's a cheap coin battery, so swap it before a big trip.",'**Name each tag clearly,** like "Blue suitcase".'],t.s)
B.bnm=new A.nd(B.c2d)
B.c3C=s([B.bzc,B.bsQ,B.bw9,B.buo,B.bnm],t.X)
B.bFT=new A.aE("8","Lost luggage",B.c3C,null)
B.byU=new A.b3("If someone else's tag travels with you, your phone warns you. iPhones do this, and so do Android phones.")
B.brR=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/find-my/fig-10.svg",760,330,"**Figure 10. What to do if you get an alert.** Find it, identify it, and if you feel unsafe, go somewhere public and call the police first.",null)
B.bpA=new A.bC(B.fi,'Why "police first" matters',"When you pull the battery, the owner stops getting updates and may notice. If you think someone is following you on purpose, keep the tag and get help before you disable it. That's our advice, not an Apple rule.",null,null,B.r)
B.bsG=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/find-my/fig-11.svg",760,194,"**Figure 11. Both phones warn you. Only Android can also scan.** An iPhone warns you on its own, but has no button to search the room on demand.",null)
B.cjH=s([B.byU,B.brR,B.bpA,B.bsG],t.X)
B.bGq=new A.aE("9","A tracker that isn't yours",B.cjH,null)
B.bAT=new A.ce("An AirTag is a GPS tracker.","It has no GPS, no Wi-Fi and no cell radio. Its location comes from iPhones that pass by.")
B.bA2=new A.ce("Apple can see where my AirTag is.","The reports are locked with a key only your devices hold.")
B.bAc=new A.ce("The map updates every few seconds.","It updates when an iPhone passes by. That can be often in an airport and never in a field.")
B.bAj=new A.ce("My iPhone can scan the room for hidden trackers.","It warns you on its own, but has no scan button. Android phones do.")
B.bAe=new A.ce("Every iPhone can point an arrow at my AirTag.","The arrow needs Ultra Wideband. Budget iPhones can still see the map and play a sound.")
B.c4u=s([B.jD,B.bAT,B.bA2,B.bAc,B.bAj,B.bAe],t.X)
B.bE4=new A.aE("10","Five things people get wrong",B.c4u,null)
B.bId=new A.aS('The \u203a symbol means "then tap". Button names can change a little between updates.',!0)
B.bwi=new A.ew("Get your devices ready")
B.cjB=s(["Open {{Settings}} \u203a {{[your name]}} \u203a {{Find My}}.","Tap {{Find My iPhone}} and turn it on.","Turn on {{Find My network}}, so the phone can be found while it's offline or switched off.","Turn on {{Send Last Location}}.","Check {{Settings}} \u203a {{Privacy & Security}} \u203a {{Location Services}} is on."],t.s)
B.bHB=new A.i_("1. Turn on Find My for your iPhone","Do this first. Without it, nothing else in this guide works for your phone.",B.cjB,null)
B.c6n=s(["Pull the plastic tab out of the AirTag. It chimes.","Hold it next to your unlocked iPhone and tap {{Connect}}.","Pick a name, or {{Custom Name}} and an emoji, then {{Continue}}.","Agree to link it to your Apple Account, then {{Done}}."],t.s)
B.bHd=new A.i_("2. Set up an AirTag","Turn on Bluetooth first. An AirTag 2 needs the latest iPhone software.",B.c6n,"If the prompt doesn't appear: {{Find My}} \u203a {{Items}} \u203a {{Add}} \u203a {{AirTag}}.")
B.ca3=s([u.o,"Tap {{Change Name and Emoji}}, choose {{Custom Name}}, type the name and pick an emoji."],t.s)
B.bHA=new A.i_("3. Change an AirTag's name or emoji",null,B.ca3,null)
B.cmc=s([u.o,"Tap {{Add Person}} below {{Share AirTag}}, choose the person and their Apple Account, and send.","To stop: tap the person's name \u203a {{Remove}}."],t.s)
