B.bvl=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/cover.svg",616,360,null,null)
B.bzs=new A.b3("A mobile hotspot takes the cell signal your phone uses and turns it into Wi-Fi. Your laptop and tablet join that Wi-Fi, just like at home. The hotspot can be a small box of its own, or your phone.")
B.bL_=new A.aS("This guide answers three questions. What is a hotspot? What makes it fast or slow? And how do you use it well?",!1)
B.bnM=new A.bC(B.ak,"A word on the words","A **cell tower** is the mast that sends and receives phone signal. **Wi-Fi** is the short-range radio your laptop uses. A **hotspot** joins the two. Here, **tethering** means sharing your phone's cell data.",null,null,B.r)
B.boI=new A.bC(B.ak,"What this guide leaves out","__Travel Routers, Explained__ covers sharing hotel Wi-Fi. __Phone Data Abroad, Explained__ covers data plans in other countries. __Weak Cell Signal at Home, Explained__ covers boosters. __Home Internet, Explained__ compares a hotspot with other ways to get internet at home.",null,null,B.r)
