B.bFO=new A.aE("1","The short answer",B.c9h,null)
B.bzi=new A.b3("A hotspot has two radios. One talks to a cell tower. The other makes Wi-Fi for your devices.")
B.bu2=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/fig-01.svg",616,404,"**Figure 1. Two radios in one box.** The cell radio brings the internet in. The Wi-Fi radio hands it out to your laptop, tablet and phone.",null)
B.bu7=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/fig-02.svg",616,210,"**Figure 2. One chain, three links.** The tower is far away. Your laptop is close. The hotspot sits in the middle and joins them.",null)
B.bSj=s([B.bzi,B.bu2,B.bu7],t.X)
B.bG4=new A.aE("2","Cell signal in, Wi-Fi out",B.bSj,null)
B.byp=new A.b3("A pocket hotspot is a small box that does only this job. Your phone can do the same job with a setting.")
B.bsS=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/fig-03.svg",616,300,"**Figure 3. Same job, two kinds.** A pocket hotspot needs its own cell service, on a SIM card or a built-in eSIM, and has its own battery. Your phone's hotspot shares the phone's.",null)
B.bs2=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/fig-04.svg",616,300,"**Figure 4. Turn it on, then join it.** On an iPhone the setting is called Personal Hotspot. On Android it's called Wi-Fi hotspot.",null)
B.ciW=s([B.byp,B.bsS,B.bs2],t.X)
B.bEx=new A.aE("3","Two kinds of hotspot",B.ciW,null)
B.by2=new A.b3("Every web page makes a round trip. It goes out through the hotspot and the tower, and comes back the same way.")
B.bsB=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/fig-05.svg",616,270,"**Figure 5. Out and back.** Your laptop asks. The hotspot passes it to the tower, and the tower sends it through the phone company's network to the website. The page comes back the same way.",null)
B.btH=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/fig-06.svg",616,214,"**Figure 6. One short link, one long one.** Wi-Fi only has to cross the table. The cell link has to reach a tower that may be across town.",null)
B.bPU=s([B.by2,B.bsB,B.btH],t.X)
B.bF3=new A.aE("4","How it works, in pictures",B.bPU,null)
B.bzz=new A.b3("Two things decide how fast a hotspot feels. The first is the cell signal where you are.")
B.bun=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/fig-07.svg",616,220,"**Figure 7. The narrow part wins.** When you sit near the hotspot, the narrow part is usually the cell link, not the Wi-Fi.",null)
B.bsb=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/fig-08.svg",616,300,"**Figure 8. Where you are matters.** Close to a tower with a clear view, the signal is strong. Far away, or behind walls, it's weak and slower.",null)
B.bHS=new A.aS("Your laptop's Wi-Fi bars show only the short link to the hotspot. To judge the speed, look at the cell bars on the hotspot or the phone. Cell bars help, but they don't promise speed. A busy tower can be slow even with full bars.",!1)
B.cmO=s([B.bzz,B.bun,B.bsb,B.bHS],t.X)
B.bFx=new A.aE("5","What decides the speed",B.cmO,null)
B.bz4=new A.b3("The second thing is how many people share the tower. A busy place can feel slow, even with full bars.")
B.bsh=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/fig-09.svg",616,300,"**Figure 9. A tower is shared.** Everyone near a tower shares it. At a game or a busy airport, there is less to go around, so many people slow down.",null)
B.buh=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/fig-10.svg",616,200,"**Figure 10. Some data waits its turn.** On some plans, when the network is busy, your data gets lower priority, so it can be slower. When it's quiet, there's no line.",null)
B.cij=s([B.bz4,B.bsh,B.buh],t.X)
B.bCJ=new A.aE("6","A busy network",B.cij,null)
B.bxR=new A.b3("A hotspot uses your cell data. A laptop can use a lot of it without asking.")
B.bti=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/fig-11.svg",616,268,"**Figure 11. Check the hotspot line.** Some plans limit hotspot data or charge extra for it. Check your plan, or ask your carrier.",null)
B.brZ=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/fig-12.svg",616,288,"**Figure 12. Turn on data saver.** Turn it on for the hotspot's network, on the device that joins it. It's called Low Data Mode on an iPhone or iPad, and Metered connection on a Windows laptop. It holds back many updates and backups, but not everything.",null)
B.bHN=new A.aS("Using a hotspot in another country? See __Phone Data Abroad, Explained__ first.",!1)
B.c4O=s([B.bxR,B.bti,B.brZ,B.bHN,B.Y4],t.X)
B.bE2=new A.aE("7","Data and your plan",B.c4O,null)
B.byw=new A.b3("Sharing data is hard work for a small radio. It uses battery, and it makes heat.")
B.bsY=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/fig-13.svg",616,270,"**Figure 13. Plug it in for long use.** On battery, a hotspot runs down fast. When it's plugged in, keep it cool and in the open. On Android, you can also set it to turn off when no one is using it.",null)
B.bvs=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/fig-14.svg",616,270,"**Figure 14. Keep it cool.** When a phone gets too hot, charging slows and its cell signal can weaken. Keep it out of the sun and out of a hot car.",null)
B.bW4=s([B.byw,B.bsY,B.bvs],t.X)
B.bG5=new A.aE("8","Battery and heat",B.bW4,null)
B.byy=new A.b3("Put the hotspot where the cell signal is best. That is often near a window, out in the open.")
B.brs=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/fig-15.svg",616,360,"**Figure 15. Near a window.** Walls and roofs weaken cell signal. A window often lets more of it in, so try a few.",null)
B.btP=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/fig-16.svg",616,212,"**Figure 16. Not in a bag.** Give it air. A bag traps heat, and heat slows it down.",null)
B.bK5=new A.aS("To find the best spot, watch the cell bars on the hotspot as you move it around. __Weak Cell Signal at Home, Explained__ has more ways to find it.",!1)
B.bMW=s([B.byy,B.brs,B.btP,B.bK5,B.HN],t.X)
B.bE8=new A.aE("9","Where to put it",B.bMW,null)
B.bxv=new A.b3("Wi-Fi is the usual way to share. A phone has two more.")
B.buR=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/fig-17.svg",616,318,"**Figure 17. Three ways to share.** Wi-Fi reaches several devices. A cable or Bluetooth reaches one.",null)
B.bUC=s(["**USB tethering:** plug a cable from your phone into one laptop. Some pairs need extra setup, and an Android phone can't do this with a Mac.","**Bluetooth tethering:** pair your phone with one nearby device, then share over Bluetooth."],t.s)
B.bnp=new A.nd(B.bUC)
B.bs5=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/fig-18.svg",616,200,"**Figure 18. Your hotspot has a name.** Anyone nearby can see it. On an iPhone, it is the phone's name: change it in Settings, General, About, Name. On Android, tap the hotspot name to change it.",null)
B.cky=s([B.bxv,B.buR,B.bnp,B.bs5],t.X)
B.bE0=new A.aE("10","Other ways to share",B.cky,null)
B.bxm=new A.b3("Your hotspot is your own small Wi-Fi network. Lock it, and turn it off when you're done.")
B.bsm=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/fig-19.svg",616,290,"**Figure 19. Use a strong password.** Some phones let you pick no password at all. Don't. Use at least eight characters, and longer is better.",null)
B.bsi=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/mobile-hotspots/fig-20.svg",616,270,"**Figure 20. Turn it off when you're done.** A device that joined before may join again by itself and use your data. Turning the hotspot off stops that.",null)
