B.bsu=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/devices-to-internet/cover.svg",700,190,null,null)
B.bxu=new A.b3("Your Wi-Fi and your internet are two different things. They meet at one box in your home. So they get blamed as one thing.")
B.buV=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/devices-to-internet/fig-01.svg",720,192,"**Figure 1. Two roads meet at one box.** Your Wi-Fi and your internet are different roads, and they meet at the box. Green is the Wi-Fi inside your home. Blue is the line out to the world.",null)
B.bIa=new A.aS("Everything you do online takes the same trip. It goes from your phone to the box, out the line you pay for, across the internet, and to the video or call you wanted. Any stop can be the slow one.",!1)
B.bnI=new A.bC(B.ak,"The one big idea","Your signal bars only measure the first hop, from your device to the box. They know nothing about the rest of the trip.",null,null,B.r)
B.bo6=new A.bC(B.ak,'A word on "the box"',"It's whatever your device talks to over the air. That might be the router your provider gave you, a gateway, or one of the mesh units around your house.",null,null,B.r)
B.ciC=s([B.bxu,B.buV,B.bIa,B.bnI,B.bo6],t.X)
B.bE5=new A.aE("1","The short answer",B.ciC,null)
B.byn=new A.b3("Here's the whole trip on one page. Every picture after this is a close-up of one part of it.")
B.buy=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/devices-to-internet/fig-02.svg",720,250,"**Figure 2. The trip.** Your device talks to the box over Wi-Fi. The box sends it out the line you pay for, across the internet, to what you wanted. Cellular goes its own way through a tower and never touches your box.",null)
B.bIJ=new A.aS("Keep this picture in mind. When something is slow, the question is always the same: which part of this trip is the slow one?",!1)
B.bQK=s([B.byn,B.buy,B.bIJ],t.X)
B.bFk=new A.aE("2","The whole trip",B.bQK,null)
B.bxb=new A.b3("The trip has two roads. The short hop through the air is your Wi-Fi. The long trip out to the world is your internet.")
B.brP=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/devices-to-internet/fig-03.svg",720,200,"**Figure 3. Two roads, one box.** The two roads meet at the box on your wall. That's why people blame them as one thing.",null)
B.bIc=new A.aS("Your internet plan pays for the second road. It does nothing for the first. If the slow part is the Wi-Fi hop, a bigger plan just costs more.",!1)
B.bJh=new A.aS("Wi-Fi gets the blame because it's the part you can see. You can see the bars and the network name. The internet road is invisible, so nobody blames it.",!1)
B.c8l=s([B.bxb,B.brP,B.bIc,B.bJh],t.X)
B.bGs=new A.aE("3","Two roads, one box",B.c8l,null)
B.bzw=new A.b3("Up close, the two roads have six stops. Any one of them can be the slow one.")
B.btl=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/devices-to-internet/fig-04.svg",720,165,"**Figure 4. Six stops.** The first three are in your home. The fourth belongs to your provider. The last two are out in the world, and nobody in your house can fix them.",null)
B.cly=s(["**Your device.** An old or busy phone can be slow on its own.","**Wi-Fi or a cable.** The short hop to the box. Walls and distance weaken Wi-Fi.","**The box.** It makes your Wi-Fi and talks to your provider. It is not the internet.","**The line you pay for.** Fiber, cable, DSL, 5G or satellite. A faster plan only changes this stop. __Home Internet, Explained__ covers each kind.","**The internet.** The networks between your provider and the world.","**The service.** The video, game, website or call you wanted."],t.s)
B.bH6=new A.hZ(B.cly)
B.bMf=s([B.bzw,B.btl,B.bH6,B.zj],t.X)
