B.bqP=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/smart-home-radios/cover.svg",700,200,null,null)
B.bzx=new A.b3("Smart home boxes use four names: Wi-Fi, Thread, Zigbee and Matter. Three of them are radios. Matter is not a radio. It's a shared language that devices speak over the radios.")
B.bKv=new A.aS("Most setup trouble comes from one thing. Many smart plugs and bulbs can only use the older 2.4 GHz part of your Wi-Fi. Your phone would rather use the faster 5 GHz part.",!1)
B.boL=new A.bC(B.ak,"The one idea that explains this guide","Matter is the language. Wi-Fi, Thread and a network cable are the ways a Matter device connects. Zigbee is an older system that reaches Matter through a bridge.",null,null,B.r)
B.c62=s([B.bzx,B.bKv,B.boL],t.X)
B.bEf=new A.aE("1","The short answer",B.c62,null)
B.bxi=new A.b3("Think of Matter as the words, and the radios as the phone lines that carry them.")
B.brm=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/smart-home-radios/fig-01.svg",720,250,"**Figure 1. Three radios and a language.** Matter devices connect by Wi-Fi, Thread or a cable. Your phone usually uses Bluetooth once, to set them up. Zigbee speaks its own language and needs a bridge.",null)
B.bud=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/smart-home-radios/fig-02.svg",760,330,"**Figure 2. The four radios in a smart home.** Wi-Fi and Thread carry Matter directly (the green row). Zigbee needs a bridge, and Bluetooth only helps at setup.",null)
B.c5D=s([B.bxi,B.brm,B.bud],t.X)
B.bFD=new A.aE("2","Three radios and a language",B.c5D,null)
B.bz5=new A.b3("All four radios use the same slice of airwaves, the 2.4 GHz band. They share it by taking turns.")
B.brS=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/smart-home-radios/fig-03.svg",700,258,"**Figure 3. One road, many lanes.** Wi-Fi uses a few wide lanes. Thread and Zigbee use many narrow ones. Each radio listens first, then talks when the lane is clear.",null)
B.bJr=new A.aS("Most homes run all of these without anyone noticing. Trouble comes when one Wi-Fi lane is busy all evening, like during a long movie. Then the small radios underneath have to wait.",!1)
B.bwq=new A.ew("Moving up helps everyone")
B.bJQ=new A.aS("Thread and Zigbee can't leave 2.4 GHz. Your phone, laptop and TV can move up to 5 or 6 GHz. Every device that moves up leaves more room for the small ones.",!1)
B.cl3=s([B.bz5,B.brS,B.bJr,B.bwq,B.bJQ],t.X)
B.bFw=new A.aE("3","One band, shared",B.cl3,null)
B.bxG=new A.b3("You plug it in, open the app, and your phone passes the plug your Wi-Fi name and password. Then the plug tries to join on its own. That's where it fails.")
B.bKH=new A.aS("Many smart plugs, bulbs and cameras have only a 2.4 GHz radio. If your Wi-Fi only offers 5 GHz, the plug can't even see it.",!1)
B.buv=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/smart-home-radios/fig-04.svg",720,140,"**Figure 4. Two bands, one name.** The plug needs 2.4 GHz to join. With one name on both bands, 2.4 GHz is there. Some setup apps also want your phone on 2.4 GHz for a minute.",null)
B.bJV=new A.aS('Some newer plugs have a 5 GHz radio too. If the box says "2.4 GHz only," it doesn\'t.',!1)
B.clY=s([B.bxG,B.bKH,B.buv,B.bJV],t.X)
