B.bxh=new A.b3("The real risks aren't about radios at all. They're older tricks.")
B.brY=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/tap-touch-near/fig-08.svg",640,344,"**Figure 8. The real risks, and what to do.** None of them is about the tap radio.",null)
B.bHI=new A.aS("**A card skimmer.** Thieves hide a fake reader in the card slot at a gas pump or a cash machine. It copies the magnetic stripe. Tap or insert your chip instead of swiping.",!1)
B.bJn=new A.aS("**A lost phone or wallet.** If your phone goes missing, mark it lost right away. On iPhone, use Find My. On Android, use Find Hub. That turns off the cards and keys stored in it. If a card goes missing, call your bank.",!1)
B.boP=new A.bC(B.fi,"Never share a code your bank texts you","Scammers call pretending to be your bank. They ask for the code that just arrived on your phone. Your bank will never ask for it. Hang up and call your bank on a number you already know.",null,null,B.r)
B.bJ5=new A.aS("One more free habit: turn on purchase alerts in your bank's app. Then a charge you didn't make shows up on your phone the same day.",!1)
B.cg5=s([B.bxh,B.brY,B.bHI,B.bJn,B.boP,B.bJ5],t.X)
B.bDx=new A.aE("5","Where the real risk is",B.cg5,null)
B.byD=new A.b3("Ultra Wideband measures distance by timing. One device sends a quick ping, the other answers, and the phone times the trip.")
B.btp=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/tap-touch-near/fig-09.svg",640,440,"**Figure 9. Your phone points the way.** It times a quick ping and reply with the tracker, then shows an arrow. Not to scale.",null)
B.bIw=new A.aS("That timing is exact. It can tell where something is to within a few centimeters (about an inch).",!1)
B.bqI=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/tap-touch-near/fig-10.svg",640,468,"**Figure 10. Two ways to judge distance.** Most Bluetooth gear guesses by how loud the signal sounds. Ultra Wideband times it, which is far more exact. Not to scale.",null)
B.bI3=new A.aS("Some newer cars use it too. Your phone can be the car key. The car checks that the phone is close before it unlocks. That stops thieves who try to pass a key's signal along from far away.",!1)
B.bvo=new A.am("assets/lesson-figures/tap-touch-near/fig-11.svg",640,420,"**Figure 11. The car checks the timing.** A signal passed along from far away takes too long, so the car stays locked. Not to scale.",null)
B.boo=new A.bC(B.ak,"Looking for your tracker?","__Find My, Explained__ covers the arrow that leads you to a lost item. __Bluetooth, Explained__ covers earbuds, speakers and your car stereo.",null,null,B.r)
B.bLc=new A.kB("bluetooth-explained",null,null)
B.bZF=s([B.byD,B.btp,B.bIw,B.bqI,B.bI3,B.bvo,B.boo,B.Y6,B.bLc],t.X)
B.bDP=new A.aE("6","Finding your keys",B.bZF,null)
B.bAi=new A.ce("Someone can read my card from across the room.","A bank card only answers a reader held right up to it. And the store has to start the payment.")
B.bAk=new A.ce("My bank cards need a blocking wallet.","They don't. Each tap uses a code that works only once. A sleeve does matter for a US passport card.")
B.bBd=new A.ce("Tapping a card is less safe than swiping it.","A phone or watch sends a stand-in number. A card does send its number, but with a one-time code, so a copied tap can't be used again.")
B.bAJ=new A.ce("Ultra Wideband is just Bluetooth.","They're different radios. Ultra Wideband times its signal to find exactly where something is.")
B.cj4=s(["**Tap or insert, don't swipe.** Especially at a gas pump.","**Pay with your phone or watch when you can.** The store never gets your card number.","**On transit, tap in and out with the same card or phone.** Keep your other tap cards away from the gate.","**Never give anyone a code your bank texts you.** Hang up and call your bank yourself.","**If your phone goes missing, mark it lost.** That switches off its cards and keys."],t.s)
B.bGG=new A.hZ(B.cj4)
