B.diu=new A.Ia("Entrance Facility (EF)","Where outside-plant and service-provider cabling enters the building. The demarcation point between the carrier and the building, usually on the lowest floor.","TIA-569 term")
B.dix=new A.Ia("Equipment Room (ER)","A larger, centralized space housing equipment that serves the whole building or campus. Often co-located with, or is, the MDF.","TIA-569 term")
B.div=new A.Ia("Telecommunications Room (TR)","The current TIA-569 term for the floor or zone space that houses the cross-connects and active gear serving a work-area zone. This is what people call an IDF or a wiring closet. One per floor at minimum, more for large floors, because horizontal runs are distance-limited.","Current standard vocabulary")
B.dit=new A.Ia("MDF (Main Distribution Frame)","Legacy term for the primary distribution point, the main equipment room, the hub. Typically the building's demarcation and entrance point for external service.","Legacy frame term, used universally")
B.dis=new A.Ia("IDF (Intermediate Distribution Frame)","Legacy term for a satellite or floor telecom room that cross-connects horizontal cabling to the backbone. Functionally the same as a TR.","Legacy frame term, used universally")
B.diw=new A.Ia("Data closet","Informal catch-all for any TR or IDF. Not a standard term at all.","Slang")
