B.a13=s(["Operator license (the GROL). The General Radiotelephone Operator License is required to adjust, maintain, or internally repair FCC-licensed transmitters in the aviation, maritime, and international-fixed-public radio services. Wi-Fi is none of those.","Equipment authorization (Part 15). This is testing and listing that a device meets FCC emission rules before it can be sold. It says the AP is legal to sell, not that a person is licensed to touch it.","Amateur (ham) license. A hobbyist authorization under Part 97. Not a commercial work credential."],t.s)
