B.c8J=s(["1. A person between the device and the AP costs decibels. The person holding the device often costs the most, because their body is right next to its antenna.","2. The loss depends on which way the holder faces. Facing the AP with the device in front costs little; turning your back puts your body in the path.","3. Crowds add up. A room full of people is a room full of obstacles that are mostly water, which is why a survey of the empty building reads better than the building in use.","4. Higher bands generally lose more to the body. The multipliers here show that trend with illustrative values, not a measured table."],t.s)
