B.df8=new A.OP(B.Mz,"2.4 GHz","2400 - 2483.5 MHz",B.vR,"83.5 MHz (US)","802.11b / g / n / ax (Wi-Fi 4 / 6)","Ch 1-11 (US) \xb7 Ch 1-13 (EU) \xb7 Ch 1-14 (JP)","3 channels at 20 MHz: 1, 6, 11","20 MHz, 40 MHz","None","Bluetooth (2.402-2.480 GHz), Zigbee (2.4 GHz), microwave ovens (~2.45 GHz), baby monitors, cordless phones","High interference environment. Best wall penetration of the three bands. Avoid as primary band in dense enterprise deployments. Wi-Fi 5 (802.11ac) does not operate in 2.4 GHz.")
B.df9=new A.OP(B.ajf,"5 GHz","5150 - 5850 MHz (US UNII-1/2A/2C/3)",B.f3,"~580 MHz usable (US UNII-1/2A/2C/3)","802.11a / n / ac / ax (Wi-Fi 5 / 6)","25 channels at 20 MHz (US, including DFS)","25 @ 20 MHz \xb7 12 @ 40 MHz \xb7 6 @ 80 MHz \xb7 2 @ 160 MHz","20 / 40 / 80 / 160 MHz","Required in UNII-2A (5250-5350 MHz) and UNII-2C (5470-5725 MHz) - radar avoidance mandatory","Weather radar, terminal Doppler radar, military radar (all managed by DFS)","UNII-1 (5150-5250 MHz): indoor use only in some regions. UNII-2A/2C require DFS - a 60-second channel availability check before first use (10 minutes for 5600-5650 MHz in the EU); on radar, leave within 10 s and stay off 30 min. UNII-3 (5725-5850 MHz): no DFS.")
B.dfa=new A.OP(B.ajg,"6 GHz","5925 - 7125 MHz",B.vS,"1200 MHz","802.11ax / be (Wi-Fi 6E / 7)","59 \xd7 20 MHz \xb7 29 \xd7 40 MHz \xb7 14 \xd7 80 MHz \xb7 7 \xd7 160 MHz \xb7 3 \xd7 320 MHz (Wi-Fi 7)","59 non-overlapping at 20 MHz \xb7 15 PSC (Preferred Scanning Channels) for APs","20 / 40 / 80 / 160 MHz (Wi-Fi 6E) \xb7 + 320 MHz (Wi-Fi 7)","No DFS - incumbent protection via AFC (Automated Frequency Coordination) for every standard-power AP, indoor or outdoor","Fixed microwave backhaul links (managed via AFC database)","Four power modes in US: Standard Power (up to 36 dBm EIRP, requires AFC indoors and outdoors) \xb7 Low Power Indoor / LPI (up to 30 dBm, no AFC) \xb7 Very Low Power / VLP (up to 14 dBm EIRP, no AFC, mobile use) \xb7 Geofenced Variable Power / GVP (up to 24 dBm EIRP, U-NII-5 and U-NII-7 only). No legacy Wi-Fi 4 or older devices - WPA3 mandatory.")
