B.a2b=s(["Static discharge damages the electronics you install: APs, switches, SFP and optics modules, line cards, and bare boards. The insidious part is latent damage. A part passes your initial test, then fails in the field weeks later.","Controls are cheap and standardized under ANSI/ESD S20.20: a grounded wrist strap, an ESD mat, and ESD-safe bags for transport. A compliant wrist strap reads in the high-kilohm to low-megohm range to ground. The risk is highest in data centers and any time you handle bare optics or boards. For a sealed AP coming out of a static bag, mounted and cabled, the risk is lower but not zero."],t.s)
