B.d4Y=new A.a7Q("802.11r","Fast BSS Transition (FT)","Folds the 4-way handshake into four frames (FT authentication and reassociation), so on a roam the client skips the full 802.1X exchange. Measured roam delay is dominated by scanning, which 802.11k shortens and FT does not (Mishra, Shin and Arbaugh 2003).","Both AP and client must support 802.11r. Must be enabled per SSID on the controller.","Essential for VoIP / UC over Wi-Fi. Some legacy clients have compatibility issues - test before deploying enterprise-wide.")
B.d4X=new A.a7Q("802.11k","Neighbor Report","AP provides the client a list of neighboring APs (BSSID, BSSID information, operating class, channel number, PHY type) so the client scans only relevant channels rather than all 40+ available.","Both AP and client must support 802.11k.","Reduces channel scan time. Does not speed up the association step itself. Works alongside 802.11r.")
B.d4Z=new A.a7Q("802.11v","BSS Transition Management","AP can suggest - or request - that a client roam to a better or less loaded AP. Primary tool for steering sticky clients.","Client must support 802.11v BSS-TM. Not all clients honor the request; behavior is client-firmware dependent.","Android and iOS generally comply. Some Windows Wi-Fi drivers ignore BSS-TM requests entirely.")
B.a3v=s([B.d4Y,B.d4X,B.d4Z],A.T("m<a7Q>"))
