B.dLn=new A.b3_("Read the spec, don\u2019t derive it.","\u201cMore gain means a narrower beam\u201d is always directionally true. The exact beamwidth that comes with a given gain depends on the specific antenna\u2019s design, so it is a rule of thumb, not a formula you can run in your head. Trust the published beamwidth on the antenna\u2019s data sheet. Don\u2019t try to back it out of the gain number.")
B.dLo=new A.b3_("Point-to-point needs real line-of-sight, not just a visible path.","The radio beam needs clearance around the straight line between the two antennas, the Fresnel zone, not only an unobstructed view. A link that looks clear to the eye can still be choked by a rooftop or a tree line sitting inside that zone.")
